# Secrets — NEVER commit
.env
# ...including backups. A copy of .env is still a copy of your credentials.
.env.bak*
.env.*.bak

# Local dev user store (contains bcrypt password hashes)
.local_users.json
.local_jobs.json
.local_jobs.json.tmp
# Autosaved script drafts (local fallback store — the user's own writing)
.local_drafts.json
# The app's own name and mark, when the local store is in use. It is a
# DEPLOYMENT's branding, not the project's — committing one deployment's name
# would rename every other checkout on its next start.
.local_branding.json
# The billboards on Explore and the wall of work under them. Same reasoning as
# the line above: these are one DEPLOYMENT's marketing copy, and committing them
# would put one installation's campaign into every other checkout.
.local_banners.json
.local_showcase.json
# Which picture sits in each of the landing hero's four tiles. Same reasoning
# again: one deployment's front page, not every checkout's.
.local_landing.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
venv/
.venv/

# Output files
output/
uploads/
*.zip

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/

# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Test screenshots — a debugging trail, not a deliverable.
# ⚠ EVERY BROWSER SUITE WRITES HERE AND ONLY HERE (`tests/_shots.py`). This
# used to be a per-suite guess at a filename in the repo root, so one failing
# test run left a dozen PNGs sitting next to `server/` and `client/` and the
# next commit swept them in. The folder is dropped whole; its README stays so a
# fresh clone still explains what the folder is for.
test_shots/*
!test_shots/README.md

# The old spellings, kept so a checkout with leftovers from before the move
# does not suddenly show them as pending.
*_probe_failed.png
row_routing_failed.png
editor_after_drop.png
restack_probe_*.png
